{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf44SMMnT7Lfv2nzG2X56","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mtp1DeCHgDfMP7GngwEHe7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 1n9doho9/.claude/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/intent.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":11304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1710},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc1bdb76-9aec-439c-aab4-d239c156bb31","uuid":"5db50822-0598-43fe-bd4e-5f55a42faa40","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:42:18.754Z","request_id":"req_011Cf44SLtFxBeKzmxLRP16b","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Mtp1DeCHgDfMP7GngwEHe7":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 1n9doho9/.claude/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/intent.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mtp1DeCHgDfMP7GngwEHe7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Intent and evidence\n2\t\n3\tRead the workspace's agent instructions, `taskspec agent-context`, and current\n4\t`taskspec status --initiative <id>` before continuing an existing initiative.\n5\tFor small, understood changes, author one TaskPlan unit or use `taskspec new` directly.\n6\tDecomposition is optional; never invent lanes to fill a template.\n7\t\n8\tFor a broader outcome, collect the desired observable result, evidence sources,\n9\tconstraints, responsible owner, and unresolved material decisions. Use\n10\t`taskspec example intent --out intent.md`, then\n11\t`taskspec decompose init <id> --intent-file intent.md`. Standard input is accepted\n12\tas `--intent-file -`. An incident JSON file can be the explicit intake source.\n13\t\n14\tResearch the repository and author the decomposition recipe. Evidence needs source\n15\tidentifiers and exact digests for local files. Missing ownership, evidence, or\n16\tmaterial decisions is a blocker to explain, not a reason to invent an answer.\n17\tExternal information remains reported until independently checked. Store decisions\n18\tin the recipe so another harness can recover them without conversation history.\n19\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc1bdb76-9aec-439c-aab4-d239c156bb31","uuid":"1546bdda-b4a5-4b94-8ca6-6c40c3f9e620","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:42:18.766Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 1n9doho9/.claude/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/intent.md","content":"# Intent and evidence\n\nRead the workspace's agent instructions, `taskspec agent-context`, and current\n`taskspec status --initiative <id>` before continuing an existing initiative.\nFor small, understood changes, author one TaskPlan unit or use `taskspec new` directly.\nDecomposition is optional; never invent lanes to fill a template.\n\nFor a broader outcome, collect the desired observable result, evidence sources,\nconstraints, responsible owner, and unresolved material decisions. Use\n`taskspec example intent --out intent.md`, then\n`taskspec decompose init <id> --intent-file intent.md`. Standard input is accepted\nas `--intent-file -`. An incident JSON file can be the explicit intake source.\n\nResearch the repository and author the decomposition recipe. Evidence needs source\nidentifiers and exact digests for local files. Missing ownership, evidence, or\nmaterial decisions is a blocker to explain, not a reason to invent an answer.\nExternal information remains reported until independently checked. Store decisions\nin the recipe so another harness can recover them without conversation history.\n","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf44SMMnT7Lfv2nzG2X56","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BAPdRtxP2soTFqwCLWBYCD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 1n9doho9/.claude/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":11304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1710},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc1bdb76-9aec-439c-aab4-d239c156bb31","uuid":"dc2ac520-88f4-4b15-af10-90eecef421c7","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:42:19.734Z","request_id":"req_011Cf44SLtFxBeKzmxLRP16b","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BAPdRtxP2soTFqwCLWBYCD":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 1n9doho9/.claude/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BAPdRtxP2soTFqwCLWBYCD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Native decomposition and review\n2\t\n3\tUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\n4\tand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\n5\tEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\n6\tstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\n7\tSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n8\t\n9\tRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\n10\tbefore recording explicit human review:\n11\t\n12\t```bash\n13\ttaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\n14\ttaskspec decompose compile <id>\n15\ttaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n16\ttaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\tReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\n20\tplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\n21\tThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\n22\tand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n23\t\n24\tBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\n25\tcompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\n26\tchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\n27\tdependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\n28\tsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n29\t\n30\tRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n31\t`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n32\t`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\n33\tAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n34\t\n35\tOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n36\t`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\n37\tor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\n38\tapplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc1bdb76-9aec-439c-aab4-d239c156bb31","uuid":"16fa936d-0bbd-4364-89e0-73bd86e0943d","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:42:19.744Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 1n9doho9/.claude/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md","content":"# Native decomposition and review\n\nUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\nand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\nEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\nstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\nSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n\nRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\nbefore recording explicit human review:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\ntaskspec decompose compile <id>\ntaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\ntaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n```\n\nReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\nplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\nThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\nand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n\nBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\ncompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\nchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\ndependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\nsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n\nRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\nAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n\nOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\nor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\napplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}}}
