{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4522KFrTEdi1LAhPCcH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I turned the blueprint into an authored decomposition recipe. Nothing was approved, sealed, or executed.\n\n## State\n\n- Initiative `rate-limit` exists at intent stage: `tasks/.plans/rate-limit/intake.md` (from `decompose init`).\n- `rate-limiting-recipe.yaml` — the proposed plan, authored against `decompose-recipe.schema.json`.\n- `intent.md` — the intake I wrote from the blueprint.\n- `decompose status rate-limit` → `DECOMPOSE=INTENT`, plan missing. No delivery plan is projected in this repo yet, for one reason given below.\n\n## Proposed topology\n\nFour seams, one swimlane each, five legs, seven leaves, strictly serial — the steel thread's order is a real dependency chain, not a scheduling preference.\n\n| Seam | Leg | Leaves |\n|---|---|---|\n| SEAM-POLICY | LEG-POLICY-VALIDATION | `policy-schema` (M) |\n| SEAM-RESOLUTION | LEG-POLICY-RESOLUTION | `policy-resolution` (M) |\n| SEAM-ENFORCEMENT | LEG-LIMIT-ENFORCEMENT | `window-counter` (M), `limit-gate` (M) |\n| SEAM-EVIDENCE | LEG-DENIAL-CONTRACT | `denial-reason` (M), `decision-telemetry` (M) |\n| SEAM-EVIDENCE | LEG-STEEL-THREAD | `steel-thread-proof` (S) |\n\nBlueprint step 3 splits into two leaves because counting in a window and deciding at the limit have separate done-conditions and separate write surfaces. `steel-thread-proof` carries `proves_capabilities` over the four preceding legs — without it the capabilities stay unproven even when every child is done. `denial-reason` and `decision-telemetry` both write `gate.py`, so they are declared as a contention serialized in steel-thread order.\n\n## Boundaries preserved\n\n- **Metering:** `DEC-METERING-BOUNDARY` is the only accepted decision cited by all four seams: metering stays provider-owned, the limiter reads and writes no provider usage counts. Every leaf repeats it as an anti-pattern and a `do_not_touch` entry, and two rejected alternatives (count from metering, emit into the metering pipeline) are recorded with reasons.\n- **Storage/deployment:** not selected. The counter sits behind an injectable store with an in-process implementation; `OBJ-INPROC-STORE` records that this proves single-process window semantics only.\n\n## Verification\n\nEvidence carries real digests: `blueprint.md` at `f40ed16c…f445`, `.taskspec/config` at `240ec604…3708`. The blueprint is recorded with claim `proposed`, since it declares itself fixture input rather than shipped behavior.\n\nValidation took four rounds — seams may cite only accepted decisions, the steel thread names legs not seams, IDs need `SEAM-`/`LANE-`/`LEG-` prefixes, and `denial-reason` at S owned three paths (raised to M). To confirm the topology itself is sound, I ran `prepare` in a scratch copy of the repo with a placeholder owner substituted; it reached `DECOMPOSE=NEEDS_REVIEW` with all 28 artifacts and `TASK_GRAPH=READY`, critical path across all seven leaves in steel-thread order. I deleted the scratch copies; that was verification, not approval.\n\n## One blocker\n\n`OBJ-NO-OWNER` is OPEN, and the engine refuses to project a delivery plan while any objection is open. The blueprint names ownership only for usage metering, which it assigns to the provider and excludes; no responsible owner is stated for the limiter work, so all four swimlanes read `unassigned pending DEC-WORK-OWNER`. I did not fill that in — assigning accountability is yours.\n\nName an owner, and this unblocks it (still stopping short of review):\n\n```\ntaskspec decompose prepare rate-limit --recipe rate-limiting-recipe.yaml\n```\n\nTwo related items I did author rather than leave open, both reviewable in the recipe: the denial reason constant `rate_limit_exceeded` (`OBJ-REASON-STRING`), and the python3/pytest layout under `src/ratelimit` (`OBJ-STACK-ASSUMED`) — the repo has no implementation source, so that layout is proposed, not observed. Reject either and the recipe needs a `--replace` revision."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":76037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":406},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc1bdb76-9aec-439c-aab4-d239c156bb31","uuid":"ed45bf80-8e21-4b4f-a59b-27cfc50d4bf7","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:50:10.978Z","request_id":"req_011Cf4521rDnGxVSWgbwNgt9"}
